  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Two multifamily apartment buildings (300 units each per phase 2 plans) and townhome-style components; up to five office/R&D buildings and three parking structures",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000508",
        "SRC-000509"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Existing 6 MW natural gas power plant to be decommissioned",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000508"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Phase 2 proposal (city page): two 300-unit apartment buildings, 122 single-family homes, 98 small-lot single-family homes, 108 townhomes, and up to 154 units in a 100% affordable building, 1,082 total; BMR units rise from 251 to 293; about 901,493 sq ft office/R&D in four buildings and about 40,000 sq ft retail (the city's June 2026 news item gives 40,629 sq ft). It would demolish about 1.4 million sq ft in 38 buildings, including Buildings P, S and T retained in the 2025 approval, and decommission the 6 MW natural gas plant. Entitlements: architectural control, conditional development permit, environmental review, heritage tree removal, BMR housing agreement, vesting tentative subdivision map.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000509",
        "SRC-002054"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Almanac (June 2026): SRI will relocate from the campus; 754 multifamily rentals unchanged; 15% of units BMR; the affordable housing developer for the 1.6-acre site had not been chosen. Parking: 1,800 spaces in two office garages, about 1.25 spaces per multifamily unit, two per townhome or single-family home, one per two affordable units. Lane Partners targets demolition start before the end of 2027.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002053"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CEQAnet NOD summary: proposed project up to 550 units (450 plus a land dedication for up to 100 affordable units); project variant adds up to 250 units, for up to 800.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002050"
      ]
    }
  ],
